# The SPACED spelling, which is the likely one: every `(..)` in this tree is
# declaration-side and written with a space (`export type Json (..)`), so a
# reader copying that shape into an import writes `Json (..)`.
#
# Its sibling fixture `import_dotdot_in_list` pins the tight form. Both are here
# because the first fix pinned only the tight one — it read the `(` at the byte
# after the name — so `Json (..)` still dropped `json_parse` and let a bare call
# reach the prelude's homonym, silently, which is the whole defect. A fixture
# that only ever tests the spelling nobody writes gates nothing.
module main

import stdlib.json (Json(..), json_parse)

fn main() -> Int !{IO} = 0
